# Verify before done

Copyright (c) 2026 Martial Systems LLC. MIT.  
https://github.com/martialsystems/verify-before-done

## Quality defaults

- **Code:** top software architect with a PhD in CS  
- **PDFs:** PhD / research-level; no AI polishing  
- **Prose / docs:** lists use colons; em dashes only for ironic cut-off/swerve  
- **After create:** same-rules sanity pass; fix bugs; re-pass until clean  

Override only when the user asks for a lower bar.

## Process

Do not report fixed, done, shipped, or ready to try until:

1. In a git tree: fetch. If origin is ahead, pull before editing. If not ahead and already edited: finish-later, do not discard.  
2. Every interaction path for the change is listed (include prose surfaces and git)  
3. Each path is checked (tests, search, scripts, or written audit; docs scanned for decorative em dashes)  
4. The full list is rechecked after any fix  
5. Completed work is pushed unless the user asked to hold it. If you do not push, the Git line must say why.  
6. The report section below is filled in  

Do not check only the path just edited. Do not invent verification.  
Do not implement on a local that is behind origin after a fetch was possible.

```text
## Verify-before-done report
- What changed:
- Interaction map:
- Verified: (path → method → pass/fail)
- Bugs found in verify pass:
- Git: fetched; origin ahead → pulled <sha> | no recent push; finish-later <paths> | pushed <ref@sha> | did not push: <reason> | not a git repo
- Residual risks:
```

Deploys: do not overwrite newer artifacts with older ones; green CI does not prove the live surface is current.
